IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nrs-dates`

-- National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) -- baseline encoding from the seat of the
-- survivor: the person who was sexually abused as a child in an institutional setting and who applies for redress,
-- receives (or does not receive) an offer, accepts or declines it, and seeks review. In ss 58-60 the seat is the person
-- asking what happens to the redress payment when the applicant dies before accepting.
--
-- SEAT. The survivor applying for redress. Questions are phrased as that person asks them. The Operator, the independent
-- decision-makers, the Ministers, the institutions and the participating jurisdictions get no seat: their opinions,
-- satisfactions and determinations ("considers", "is satisfied", "determines") are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, a number, a date, a choice from a list). No question takes a DEONTIC or an
-- EVENT. The three steps with a deadline (s 42(3) my acceptance document; s 73(2)(a) my application for review; Rules
-- s 15(2) the Operator's notice to a child applicant before turning 18) are regulative rules run inside a question.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: ss 6 (definitions used), 12-17, 19-22, 24(4), 26(1), 28, 29(1)-(3), 30, 31(2), 34(4)-(10),
-- 37, 39, 40, 42, 43, 45, 49, 50, 51(2)-(3), 52, 53, 54, 56B, 56C, 56D, 58-61, 63, 64, 73, 75(4), 78, 167, 193(1); and
-- the National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Rules 2018 ss 4B, 6, 11, 12, 15, 26(3)-(5).
-- What is out, and why, is in NOTES.md.
--
-- Edition: National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018, No. 45, 2018, Compilation No. 9,
-- compilation date 28 September 2024 (register id C2024C00613), deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C2018A00045.txt
-- (the s 30(2) formula from C2018A00045.formulas.md). Rules: Compilation No. 9, compilation date 19 February 2025
-- (register id F2025C00180), deposited at
-- ../../../national-redress-scheme-for-institutional-child-sexual-abuse-rules-2018/registers/source-bundle/F2018L00975.txt.
-- The assessment framework (s 32) is not deposited: the amounts it gives are inputs.
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. Answers follow the rulings on negatives of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05
-- (NOTES.md): JUST FALSE is the text's own no; NOTHING is where the text is silent or limited by its own wording.

§ `National Redress Scheme Act 2018 -- the survivor`

DECLARE `Redress party` IS ONE OF `I, the survivor applying for redress`, `the Operator`
DECLARE `Redress step` IS ONE OF
    `give the Operator my acceptance document`
    `apply for review of the Operator's determination`
    `give me the notice before I turn 18` HAS `given on day` IS A NUMBER

-- s 16(1)(a), s 30(2) step 1: the redress payment is "of up to $150,000"; the maximum amount "must not be more than
-- $150,000, regardless of the number of responsible institutions".
`the cap on the maximum amount` MEANS 150000

-- s 16(1)(b)(ii), s 31(2): the counselling and psychological component "must not be more than $5,000".
`the cap on the counselling and psychological component` MEANS 5000

-- s 56B(2): "The amount of the advance payment is $10,000."
`the amount of an advance payment` MEANS 10000

§§ `Can I apply (Part 2-3 Division 2; s 193)`

-- s 19(1): "To obtain redress under the scheme, a person must make an application to the Operator." s 20(1): "A person
-- cannot make an application for redress under the scheme if: (a) the person has already made an application ...; or
-- (b) a security notice is in force in relation to the person; or (c) the person is a child who will not turn 18 before
-- the scheme sunset day; or (e) the application is being made in the period of 12 months before the scheme sunset day."
-- (2): "(1)(e) does not apply if the Operator determines there are exceptional circumstances". s 22(2): a withdrawn
-- application "is treated as not having been made". s 193(1): the Act ceases to have effect at the end of the scheme
-- sunset day.
DECLARE `Whether I can apply for redress` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I can apply to the Operator (s 19)`
    `yes, as a child: the Operator must deal with my application under the special process for child applicants and cannot decide it before I turn 18 (s 21; Rules s 15)`
    `yes: the application falls in the last 12 months before the scheme sunset day, but the Operator has determined there are exceptional circumstances (s 20(2))`
    `no: I have already made an application; only one withdrawn before it was decided does not count (ss 20(1)(a), 22(2))`
    `no: a security notice is in force in relation to me (s 20(1)(b))`
    `no: I am a child who will not turn 18 before the scheme sunset day (s 20(1)(c))`
    `no: the application would be made in the 12 months before the scheme sunset day, and the Operator has not determined exceptional circumstances (s 20(1)(e), (2))`
    `no: the scheme has ended; the Act ceased to have effect at the end of the scheme sunset day (s 193(1))`
    `not covered: the day is before the scheme start day, 1 July 2018`

GIVEN `applying on` IS A DATE, `my date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6 -- I am a child on the day` `applying on` `my date of birth` IF
    `the day` `applying on` `is before` (`the day I turn 18` `my date of birth`)

-- The 12 months before the scheme sunset day: 1 July 2027 to 30 June 2028 (fork F1: the sunset day itself is not in it).
GIVEN `applying on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20(1)(e) -- in the 12 months before the scheme sunset day` `applying on` IF
        `the day` `applying on` `is on or after` (`the same day` (0 MINUS 12) `months on from` `the scheme sunset day`)
    AND `the day` `applying on` `is before` `the scheme sunset day`

@export Can I apply for redress under the National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 19-22, 193)? You can make only one application. You cannot apply while a security notice is in force, as a child who will not turn 18 before the scheme ends (1 July 2028), or in the last 12 months before the scheme ends (from 1 July 2027) unless the Operator decides there are exceptional circumstances. An application you withdrew before it was decided does not count.
GIVEN `applying on` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply, or would apply, for redress
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `I have already applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have already made an application for redress under the scheme (do not count one you withdrew before the Operator decided it)
      `a security notice is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a security notice from the Home Affairs Minister is in force in relation to you
      `exceptional circumstances determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator has determined that there are exceptional circumstances justifying your application being made in the last 12 months before the scheme ends
GIVETH A `Whether I can apply for redress`
`Can I apply for redress question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day` `applying on` `is before` `the scheme start day`
              THEN `not covered: the day is before the scheme start day, 1 July 2018`
           IF `the day` `applying on` `is after` `the scheme sunset day`
              THEN `no: the scheme has ended; the Act ceased to have effect at the end of the scheme sunset day (s 193(1))`
           IF `I have already applied`
              THEN `no: I have already made an application; only one withdrawn before it was decided does not count (ss 20(1)(a), 22(2))`
           IF `a security notice is in force`
              THEN `no: a security notice is in force in relation to me (s 20(1)(b))`
           IF `s 6 -- I am a child on the day` `applying on` `my date of birth` AND `the day` (`the day I turn 18` `my date of birth`) `is on or after` `the scheme sunset day`
              THEN `no: I am a child who will not turn 18 before the scheme sunset day (s 20(1)(c))`
           IF `s 20(1)(e) -- in the 12 months before the scheme sunset day` `applying on` AND (NOT `exceptional circumstances determined`)
              THEN `no: the application would be made in the 12 months before the scheme sunset day, and the Operator has not determined exceptional circumstances (s 20(1)(e), (2))`
           IF `s 6 -- I am a child on the day` `applying on` `my date of birth`
              THEN `yes, as a child: the Operator must deal with my application under the special process for child applicants and cannot decide it before I turn 18 (s 21; Rules s 15)`
           IF `s 20(1)(e) -- in the 12 months before the scheme sunset day` `applying on`
              THEN `yes: the application falls in the last 12 months before the scheme sunset day, but the Operator has determined there are exceptional circumstances (s 20(2))`
           OTHERWISE `yes: I can apply to the Operator (s 19)`

DECLARE `My last day to apply` IS ONE OF
    `my last day to apply, without needing the Operator to find exceptional circumstances, is` HAS `the last ordinary day` IS A DATE
    `none: I will be a child until on or after the scheme sunset day, so I cannot apply as a child (s 20(1)(c)), and once I turn 18 the last 12 months have begun (s 20(1)(e))`

@export What is the last day I can apply for redress (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 20, 193)? The scheme ends at the end of 1 July 2028 (the tenth anniversary of its start on 1 July 2018). Applications cannot be made in the 12 months before that day unless the Operator decides there are exceptional circumstances, so the last ordinary day is 30 June 2027. The day is not moved if it falls on a weekend or public holiday.
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
GIVETH A `My last day to apply`
`What is my last day to apply for redress question` MEANS
    IF `the day` (`the day I turn 18` `my date of birth`) `is on or after` `the scheme sunset day`
    THEN `none: I will be a child until on or after the scheme sunset day, so I cannot apply as a child (s 20(1)(c)), and once I turn 18 the last 12 months have begun (s 20(1)(e))`
    ELSE `my last day to apply, without needing the Operator to find exceptional circumstances, is` (`the date` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` (`the same day` (0 MINUS 12) `months on from` `the scheme sunset day`))

§§ `Am I eligible (Part 2-2; Part 3-1 Division 3; Rules Parts 1A, 2, 3)`

DECLARE `Where the abuse occurred` IS ONE OF
    `inside a participating State`
    `inside a Territory`
    `outside Australia`
    `inside a State that is not a participating State`

DECLARE `Whether my abuse is within the scope of the scheme` IS ONE OF
    `within the scope of the scheme (s 14(1))`
    `within the scope through s 61: it occurred in a non-participating State, but a Commonwealth or participating Territory institution is primarily responsible; it counts if I am otherwise eligible (s 61(1), (2))`
    `not within the scope: I was not a child when it occurred (s 14(1)(a))`
    `not within the scope: it occurred on or after the scheme start day, 1 July 2018 (s 14(1)(c))`
    `not within the scope: it occurred in a State that is not a participating State, and no Commonwealth or participating Territory institution is primarily responsible (ss 14(1)(b), 61)`
    `not within the scope: it was sexual abuse by a child that did not involve physical contact with me or penetration of me (Rules s 6)`

-- s 14(1): "Abuse of a person is within the scope of the scheme if: (a) it occurred when the person was a child; and
-- (b) it occurred: (i) inside a participating State; or (ii) inside a Territory; or (iii) outside Australia; and (c) it
-- occurred before the scheme start day." (3): "not within the scope ... if this Act or the rules prescribe". Rules s 6:
-- "sexual abuse of a person by a child is not within the scope of the scheme if the abuse did not involve physical
-- contact with, or penetration of, the person." s 61(2): within the scope if the person is eligible because of s 61(1).
-- Which States are participating States is set by s 144 and the States' referral Acts (not deposited): asked as a fact.
@export Is the abuse I suffered within the scope of the National Redress Scheme (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 14, 61; Rules s 6)? Abuse is within the scope if it happened when you were under 18, before 1 July 2018, and inside a participating State, inside a Territory, or outside Australia. Abuse in a State that has not joined the scheme can still count if a Commonwealth or participating Territory institution is primarily responsible. Sexual abuse by another child is outside the scope if it involved no physical contact or penetration.
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the abuse occurred on` IS A DATE @desc The day the abuse occurred (for abuse over a period, ask once for each occasion that matters)
      `where it occurred` IS A `Where the abuse occurred` @desc Where the abuse occurred: inside a State that participates in the scheme, inside a Territory, outside Australia, or inside a State that does not participate
      `a Commonwealth or participating Territory institution is primarily responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Commonwealth institution, or an institution of the ACT or the Northern Territory, is primarily responsible for the abuse (that is, solely or primarily responsible for the abuser having contact with you)
      `the abuser was a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuser was under 18 at the time
      `there was physical contact or penetration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse involved physical contact with you or penetration of you
GIVETH A `Whether my abuse is within the scope of the scheme`
`Is my abuse within the scope of the scheme question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`s 6 -- I am a child on the day` `the abuse occurred on` `my date of birth`)
              THEN `not within the scope: I was not a child when it occurred (s 14(1)(a))`
           IF `the day` `the abuse occurred on` `is on or after` `the scheme start day`
              THEN `not within the scope: it occurred on or after the scheme start day, 1 July 2018 (s 14(1)(c))`
           IF `the abuser was a child` AND (NOT `there was physical contact or penetration`)
              THEN `not within the scope: it was sexual abuse by a child that did not involve physical contact with me or penetration of me (Rules s 6)`
           IF `where it occurred` EQUALS `inside a State that is not a participating State` AND `a Commonwealth or participating Territory institution is primarily responsible`
              THEN `within the scope through s 61: it occurred in a non-participating State, but a Commonwealth or participating Territory institution is primarily responsible; it counts if I am otherwise eligible (s 61(1), (2))`
           IF `where it occurred` EQUALS `inside a State that is not a participating State`
              THEN `not within the scope: it occurred in a State that is not a participating State, and no Commonwealth or participating Territory institution is primarily responsible (ss 14(1)(b), 61)`
           OTHERWISE `within the scope of the scheme (s 14(1))`

DECLARE `Who is responsible for the abuse` IS ONE OF
    `a participating institution`
    `an institution listed for a participating jurisdiction under s 164A, 164B or 164C, and a participating jurisdiction is an eligible funding jurisdiction for it`
    `no participating institution and no such listed institution`

-- Rules s 4B(2): the child migrant from the United Kingdom or Malta, who is eligible without being a citizen or
-- permanent resident (s 4B(1)(e) replaces s 13(1)(e)).
GIVEN `sent before 1984 from the UK or Malta with no family here but children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the Empire Settlement scheme or a ward under the 1946 Act or regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `became a ward of a participating State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `abused while a ward` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Rules s 4B(2) -- a child migrant` `sent before 1984 from the UK or Malta with no family here but children` `under the Empire Settlement scheme or a ward under the 1946 Act or regulations` `became a ward of a participating State or Territory` `abused while a ward` IF
        `sent before 1984 from the UK or Malta with no family here but children`
    AND `under the Empire Settlement scheme or a ward under the 1946 Act or regulations`
    AND `became a ward of a participating State or Territory`
    AND `abused while a ward`

-- s 13(1): "A person is eligible for redress under the scheme if: (a) the person was sexually abused; and (b) the sexual
-- abuse is within the scope of the scheme ...; and (c) the sexual abuse is of a kind for which the maximum amount of
-- redress payment ... (as worked out under the assessment framework) would be more than nil; and (d) one or more of the
-- following are responsible for the abuse: (i) a participating institution; (ii) an institution that is listed ... under
-- section 164A, 164B or 164C (if a participating jurisdiction is an eligible funding jurisdiction ...); and (e) the
-- person is an Australian citizen or a permanent resident ... at the time the person applies". (2): also eligible if
-- the Act or the rules prescribe (s 61; Rules s 4B). s 61(1): eligible if eligible apart from the abuse being in a
-- non-participating State, and "a Commonwealth institution or a participating Territory institution is primarily
-- responsible". JUST TRUE eligible; JUST FALSE where the conditions fail (fork F2: s 13(2) leaves room for rules made later).
@export Am I eligible for redress under the National Redress Scheme (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 13, 14, 61; Rules ss 4B, 6)? You are eligible if you were sexually abused as a child, the abuse is within the scope of the scheme, the assessment framework would give it an amount above nil, a participating institution (or an institution listed for a funder of last resort) is responsible, and you are an Australian citizen or permanent resident when you apply. Certain child migrants from the United Kingdom and Malta do not need to be citizens or permanent residents. The Operator decides this on whether there is a reasonable likelihood that you are eligible.
GIVEN `I was sexually abused` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were sexually abused (redress also covers related non-sexual abuse, but there must have been sexual abuse)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the abuse occurred on` IS A DATE @desc The day the sexual abuse occurred
      `where it occurred` IS A `Where the abuse occurred` @desc Where the sexual abuse occurred
      `a Commonwealth or participating Territory institution is primarily responsible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a Commonwealth institution, or an institution of the ACT or the Northern Territory, is primarily responsible for the abuse
      `the abuser was a child` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuser was under 18 at the time
      `there was physical contact or penetration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse involved physical contact with you or penetration of you
      `more than nil under the assessment framework` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse is of a kind for which the assessment framework would give a maximum redress payment above nil
      `who is responsible` IS A `Who is responsible for the abuse` @desc Which kind of institution is responsible for the abuse: a participating institution; an institution listed for a participating jurisdiction under s 164A, 164B or 164C that has a participating jurisdiction as funder; or neither
      `citizen or permanent resident when I applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were an Australian citizen or permanent resident on the day you applied
      `sent before 1984 from the UK or Malta with no family here but children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you arrived in Australia before 1984 as a child sent from the United Kingdom or Malta by an institution, with no family members in Australia other than children
      `under the Empire Settlement scheme or a ward under the 1946 Act or regulations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were sent under a scheme under the Empire Settlement Act 1922 (UK), or became a ward under the National Security (Overseas Children) Regulations or the Immigration (Guardianship of Children) Act 1946
      `became a ward of a participating State or Territory` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became a ward of a participating State or Territory
      `abused while a ward` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse occurred while you were that ward
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I eligible for redress question` MEANS
    IF      `I was sexually abused`
        AND `in scope`
        AND `more than nil under the assessment framework`
        AND (NOT (`who is responsible` EQUALS `no participating institution and no such listed institution`))
        AND (`citizen or permanent resident when I applied` OR (`a child migrant` AND (NOT `through s 61`)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `the scope answer` MEANS `Is my abuse within the scope of the scheme question` `my date of birth` `the abuse occurred on` `where it occurred` `a Commonwealth or participating Territory institution is primarily responsible` `the abuser was a child` `there was physical contact or penetration`
        `through s 61` MEANS `the scope answer` EQUALS `within the scope through s 61: it occurred in a non-participating State, but a Commonwealth or participating Territory institution is primarily responsible; it counts if I am otherwise eligible (s 61(1), (2))`
        `in scope` MEANS
               `the scope answer` EQUALS `within the scope of the scheme (s 14(1))`
            OR `through s 61`
        `a child migrant` MEANS `Rules s 4B(2) -- a child migrant` `sent before 1984 from the UK or Malta with no family here but children` `under the Empire Settlement scheme or a ward under the 1946 Act or regulations` `became a ward of a participating State or Territory` `abused while a ward`

DECLARE `How the institution stands to the abuser's contact with me` IS ONE OF
    `solely or primarily responsible for the abuser having contact with me`
    `approximately equally responsible with one or more other institutions, and no institution is primarily responsible`
    `neither`

DECLARE `Whether the institution is responsible for my abuse` IS ONE OF
    `responsible: primarily responsible (s 15(1), (2))`
    `responsible: equally responsible (s 15(1), (3))`
    `not responsible: a court ordered it to pay me compensation or damages for the abuse (Rules s 11)`
    `not responsible: it is a government authority whose only connection with the abuse is that it regulated, funded or established the other institution (Rules s 12)`
    `not responsible (s 15(1))`

-- s 15(1): "An institution ... is responsible for abuse of a person if the institution is primarily responsible or
-- equally responsible". (2): primarily responsible "if the institution is solely or primarily responsible for the abuser
-- having contact with the person". (3): equally responsible if "approximately equally responsible" with others and "no
-- institution is primarily responsible". (4): relevant circumstances, none on its own determinative: a judgment for the
-- Operator, asked as a finding. (6), Rules s 11: an institution a court ordered (other than by consent) to pay
-- compensation or damages for the abuse, not set aside on appeal, is not responsible. Rules s 12(2): a government authority
-- "is not responsible" where "the only connection ... is" regulating, funding or establishing the other institution
-- (subject to Rules Part 3 Division 2, ss 8-10, which are out: NOTES.md).
@export Is an institution responsible for my abuse under the National Redress Scheme (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) s 15; Rules ss 11, 12)? An institution is responsible if it was solely or primarily responsible for the abuser having contact with you, or approximately equally responsible with other institutions where none is primarily responsible. Relevant circumstances include care or custody, guardianship, placement, whether the abuser was its official, and whether the abuse happened on its premises or in its activities. An institution a court has ordered to pay you damages for the abuse is not responsible, nor is a government authority that only regulated, funded or set up the institution where the abuse happened.
GIVEN `how it stands` IS A `How the institution stands to the abuser's contact with me` @desc How the Operator finds this institution stood to the abuser having contact with you: solely or primarily responsible; approximately equally responsible with others where none is primarily responsible; or neither
      `a court ordered it to pay me damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a court ordered (other than by consent) this institution to pay you, or a group including you, compensation or damages for the abuse, the order was not set aside on appeal, and you did not choose to refuse your share
      `a government authority that only regulated, funded or established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this institution is a Commonwealth, State or Territory authority whose only connection with the abuse is that it regulated or funded the institution where the abuse happened (or its activity), or that the institution was set up under its jurisdiction's law
GIVETH A `Whether the institution is responsible for my abuse`
`Is the institution responsible for my abuse question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a court ordered it to pay me damages`
              THEN `not responsible: a court ordered it to pay me compensation or damages for the abuse (Rules s 11)`
           IF `a government authority that only regulated, funded or established`
              THEN `not responsible: it is a government authority whose only connection with the abuse is that it regulated, funded or established the other institution (Rules s 12)`
           IF `how it stands` EQUALS `solely or primarily responsible for the abuser having contact with me`
              THEN `responsible: primarily responsible (s 15(1), (2))`
           IF `how it stands` EQUALS `approximately equally responsible with one or more other institutions, and no institution is primarily responsible`
              THEN `responsible: equally responsible (s 15(1), (3))`
           OTHERWISE `not responsible (s 15(1))`

§§ `After I apply (Part 2-3 Divisions 3 and 4; Rules s 15)`

-- s 24(4): "The production period must be at least: (a) if the Operator considers the application is urgent--4 weeks;
-- and (b) otherwise--8 weeks; beginning on the date of the notice." (7): a request to extend "must ... be made before the
-- end of the production period". s 26(1): if the information is not provided in the production period, "the Operator is
-- not required to make a determination on the application until the information is provided".
@export The Operator has asked me for more information about my redress application: what is the shortest time it may give me (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 24, 26)? The period must be at least 4 weeks if the Operator considers the application urgent, and otherwise at least 8 weeks, beginning on the date of the notice. You may ask for an extension before the period ends. If you do not give the information in time, the Operator need not decide your application until you do. The answer is the earliest day the period may end; the notice may give you longer.
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date of the Operator's written notice asking you for information
      `the Operator considers my application urgent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator considers your application urgent
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the earliest my time to give information can end question` MEANS
    IF `the Operator considers my application urgent`
    THEN `the date` 27 `days after` `the date of the notice`
    ELSE `the date` 55 `days after` `the date of the notice`

DECLARE `What the Operator must do with my application` IS ONE OF
    `not required to decide it: my application is not valid (s 19(2), (3))`
    `not yet: I have not given information the Operator asked for within the production period; it need not decide until I do (s 26(1))`
    `not yet: I applied as a child; the Operator must not decide before I turn 18, and must decide as soon as practicable after (s 21; Rules s 15(3), (4))`
    `must approve my application and give me a written offer of redress (ss 29(2), 39)`
    `must decide not to approve my application (s 29(3)); I may apply for review (s 73)`

-- s 29(1): "the Operator must make a determination to approve, or not approve, the application as soon as practicable."
-- (2): "If the Operator considers that there is a reasonable likelihood that the person is eligible for redress, then the
-- Operator must: (a) approve the application". (3): "Otherwise, the Operator must make a determination not to approve".
-- s 6: "reasonable likelihood ... means the chance of the person being eligible is real, is not fanciful or remote and is
-- more than merely plausible." s 39: if approved, the Operator "must give the person a written offer of redress".
@export What must the Operator do with my redress application (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 19, 21, 26, 29, 39; Rules s 15)? The Operator must decide as soon as practicable. If it considers there is a reasonable likelihood that you are eligible (a real chance, not fanciful or remote, more than merely plausible), it must approve your application and make you an offer; otherwise it must decide not to approve it. It need not decide an invalid application, or one where you have not given information it asked for in time. An application made as a child cannot be decided before you turn 18.
GIVEN `my application is valid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application is in the approved form, says where you live, and includes the information and documents the Operator requires
      `information I was asked for is overdue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator asked you for information and you did not give it within the period in the notice (and have not given it since)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `applied on` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
      `the Operator considers there is a reasonable likelihood I am eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator considers there is a reasonable likelihood that you are eligible for redress
GIVETH A `What the Operator must do with my application`
`What must the Operator do with my application question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `my application is valid`
              THEN `not required to decide it: my application is not valid (s 19(2), (3))`
           IF `information I was asked for is overdue`
              THEN `not yet: I have not given information the Operator asked for within the production period; it need not decide until I do (s 26(1))`
           IF `s 6 -- I am a child on the day` `applied on` `my date of birth` AND `s 6 -- I am a child on the day` `today` `my date of birth`
              THEN `not yet: I applied as a child; the Operator must not decide before I turn 18, and must decide as soon as practicable after (s 21; Rules s 15(3), (4))`
           IF `the Operator considers there is a reasonable likelihood I am eligible`
              THEN `must approve my application and give me a written offer of redress (ss 29(2), 39)`
           OTHERWISE `must decide not to approve my application (s 29(3)); I may apply for review (s 73)`

-- Rules s 15(2): "If the application is made at least 4 months before the day the person turns 18, the Operator must give
-- the person a notice at least 3 months, but not more than 6 months, before that day". As a regulative rule, counted in
-- days from the day of the application; a notice outside the window does not count (PROVIDED).
GIVEN `the first day of the window` IS A NUMBER, `the last day of the window` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Redress party` `Redress step`
`Rules s 15(2) -- the Operator must give me my notice before I turn 18` `the first day of the window` `the last day of the window` MEANS
    PARTY `the Operator`
    MUST `give me the notice before I turn 18` `the day it is given` PROVIDED `the day it is given` AT LEAST `the first day of the window`
    WITHIN `the last day of the window`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the Operator` BECAUSE "no notice in the window from 6 months to 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2)); the Operator must still not decide before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(3))"

GIVEN `the first day of the window` IS A NUMBER, `the last day of the window` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Rules s 15(2) -- a notice on this day is in time` `the first day of the window` `the last day of the window` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`Rules s 15(2) -- the Operator must give me my notice before I turn 18` `the first day of the window` `the last day of the window`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `the Operator` (`give me the notice before I turn 18` `the day`) `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Where my notice before turning 18 stands` IS ONE OF
    `no notice is required: I was not a child when I applied`
    `no notice is required: I applied less than 4 months before turning 18 (Rules s 15(2))`
    `given in time`
    `not yet due: the Operator has until 3 months before I turn 18`
    `late: no notice in the window from 6 months to 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2))`

@export I applied for redress as a child: has the Operator given me the notice it must give before I turn 18 (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) s 21; Rules s 15)? If you applied at least 4 months before turning 18, the Operator must tell you, between 6 months and 3 months before your 18th birthday, that your application will be decided as soon as practicable after you turn 18, and invite you to give any further information before then. A notice given earlier than 6 months before does not count.
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `applied on` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied
      `the notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator has given you this notice
      `the notice was given on` IS A DATE @desc The day it was given (if not given, any date; it is not used)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where my notice before turning 18 stands`
`Has the Operator given me my notice before I turn 18 question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`s 6 -- I am a child on the day` `applied on` `my date of birth`)
              THEN `no notice is required: I was not a child when I applied`
           IF `the day` `applied on` `is after` (`the same day` (0 MINUS 4) `months on from` `the 18th birthday`)
              THEN `no notice is required: I applied less than 4 months before turning 18 (Rules s 15(2))`
           IF `the notice was given` AND `Rules s 15(2) -- a notice on this day is in time` `window opens` `window closes` (`the days from` `applied on` `to` `the notice was given on`)
              THEN `given in time`
           IF `the day` `today` `is on or before` `the window's last day`
              THEN `not yet due: the Operator has until 3 months before I turn 18`
           OTHERWISE `late: no notice in the window from 6 months to 3 months before I turn 18 (Rules s 15(2))`
    WHERE
        `the 18th birthday` MEANS `the day I turn 18` `my date of birth`
        `the window's last day` MEANS `the same day` (0 MINUS 3) `months on from` `the 18th birthday`
        `window opens` MEANS `the days from` `applied on` `to` (`the same day` (0 MINUS 6) `months on from` `the 18th birthday`)
        `window closes` MEANS `the days from` `applied on` `to` `the window's last day`

§§ `How much I get (ss 16, 30, 31, 51, 56B; Rules s 26)`

DECLARE `Relevant prior payment` HAS
    `original amount` IS A NUMBER
    `paid to me on` IS A DATE

DECLARE `Responsible institution` HAS
    `gross liability amount` IS A NUMBER
    `its relevant prior payments` IS A LIST OF `Relevant prior payment`

-- s 30(2) step 4 (formula from C2018A00045.formulas.md): "Multiply the original amount by the following: (1.019)^n where:
-- n is the number of whole years since the relevant prior payment was paid to the person."
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`1.019 to the power` n MEANS
    IF n AT MOST 0
    THEN 1
    ELSE 1.019 TIMES (`1.019 to the power` (n MINUS 1))

GIVEN p IS A `Relevant prior payment`, `the counting day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 30(2) step 4 -- the adjusted amount of` p `counted to` `the counting day` MEANS
    p's `original amount` TIMES (`1.019 to the power` (`the whole years from` (p's `paid to me on`) `to` `the counting day`))

-- s 30(2) step 5: "Add together the adjusted amount of each relevant prior payment ... If the resulting amount is not a
-- whole number of cents, round the amount up to the next whole number of cents. This amount is the reduction amount".
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded up to the next whole cent` x MEANS (CEILING (x TIMES 100)) DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN i IS A `Responsible institution`, `the counting day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 30(2) step 5 -- the reduction amount for` i `counted to` `the counting day` MEANS
    `rounded up to the next whole cent` (sum (map (GIVEN p YIELD `s 30(2) step 4 -- the adjusted amount of` p `counted to` `the counting day`) (i's `its relevant prior payments`)))

-- s 30(2) step 6: the share "is the gross liability amount ... less the reduction amount ... The amount may be nil but
-- not less than nil."
GIVEN i IS A `Responsible institution`, `the counting day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 30(2) step 6 -- the institution's share` i `counted to` `the counting day` MEANS
    max 0 ((i's `gross liability amount`) MINUS (`s 30(2) step 5 -- the reduction amount for` i `counted to` `the counting day`))

-- s 30(3): the institutions' total share.
GIVEN `the institutions` IS A LIST OF `Responsible institution`
      `the counting day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 30(3) -- the institutions' total share` `the institutions` `counted to` `the counting day` MEANS
    sum (map (GIVEN i YIELD `s 30(2) step 6 -- the institution's share` i `counted to` `the counting day`) `the institutions`)

-- s 30(4): the Commonwealth's share "is the difference between: (a) the institutions' total share ...; and (b)" the total
-- share with n counted only to the day the person applied. The counting date in (a) is the day of the determination.
GIVEN `the institutions` IS A LIST OF `Responsible institution`
      `applied on` IS A DATE
      `determined on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 30(4) -- the Commonwealth's share` `the institutions` `applied on` `determined on` MEANS
    IF `at application` AT LEAST `at determination`
    THEN `at application` MINUS `at determination`
    ELSE `at determination` MINUS `at application`
    WHERE
        `at application` MEANS `s 30(3) -- the institutions' total share` `the institutions` `counted to` `applied on`
        `at determination` MEANS `s 30(3) -- the institutions' total share` `the institutions` `counted to` `determined on`

-- s 30(5): the redress payment is the institutions' total share plus the Commonwealth's share, less any advance payment;
-- "may be nil but not less than nil".
GIVEN `the institutions` IS A LIST OF `Responsible institution`
      `applied on` IS A DATE
      `determined on` IS A DATE
      `the advance payment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 30(5) -- the amount of my redress payment` `the institutions` `applied on` `determined on` `the advance payment` MEANS
    max 0 (((`s 30(3) -- the institutions' total share` `the institutions` `counted to` `determined on`) PLUS (`s 30(4) -- the Commonwealth's share` `the institutions` `applied on` `determined on`)) MINUS `the advance payment`)

-- The question, for the common case of one responsible institution that is the only institution responsible (Rules
-- s 21(1) note: its share of the maximum amount is then the whole of it) and at most one relevant prior payment.
@export How much redress payment will I get, where one participating institution is responsible for my abuse (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 16, 30)? The maximum amount under the assessment framework (at most $150,000) is reduced by any earlier payment the institution made to you for the abuse, increased by 1.9% for each whole year from when it was paid to when you applied (the Commonwealth bears the increase for the years while your application is processed), and by any $10,000 advance payment. The result may be nil but not less. Enter the maximum amount the assessment framework gives, as the framework is not part of this encoding, and the part of any earlier payment that counts (see the question on earlier payments).
GIVEN `the maximum amount under the assessment framework` IS A NUMBER @desc The maximum redress payment the assessment framework gives for your abuse, in dollars, before any earlier or advance payment is taken off (the Act caps it at 150000)
      `I received an earlier payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the responsible institution (or someone on its behalf) paid you an earlier amount for the abuse that counts as a relevant prior payment
      `the part of it that counts` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of that earlier payment that counts as a relevant prior payment, in dollars (0 if none)
      `it was paid on` IS A DATE @desc The day the earlier payment was paid to you (if none, any date; it is not used)
      `I applied on` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied for redress
      `determined on` IS A DATE @desc The day the Operator decides (or decided) your application
      `I received an advance payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were paid the $10,000 advance payment
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much redress payment will I get question` MEANS
    `s 30(5) -- the amount of my redress payment` (LIST `the institution`) `I applied on` `determined on` `the advance`
    WHERE
        `the payments` MEANS
            IF `I received an earlier payment`
            THEN LIST (`Relevant prior payment` WITH `original amount` IS `the part of it that counts`, `paid to me on` IS `it was paid on`)
            ELSE EMPTY
        `the institution` MEANS `Responsible institution` WITH `gross liability amount` IS (min `the cap on the maximum amount` `the maximum amount under the assessment framework`), `its relevant prior payments` IS `the payments`
        `the advance` MEANS
            IF `I received an advance payment`
            THEN `the amount of an advance payment`
            ELSE 0

-- s 30(2) step 3: a relevant prior payment is a payment "paid to the person by, or on behalf of, the responsible
-- institution in relation to abuse for which the institution is responsible (but do not include any payment to the
-- extent that it is prescribed by the rules as not being a relevant prior payment)". Rules s 26(3): payments under the
-- listed compensation Acts are "not a relevant prior payment (to any extent)"; (4): "not ... to the extent that (a) it is
-- not in recognition of (i) the abuse; or (ii) harm caused by the abuse; or (b) it is reasonably attributable to (i)
-- expenses of medical, dental or other treatment; or (ii) any other expenses"; (5): a payment for non-sexual abuse not
-- covered by a set of abuse that also covers sexual abuse is not a relevant prior payment. (6): the split of a payment made
-- for two or more responsible institutions is by a formula the deposit lost; that case answers NOTHING.
@export How much of a payment I received earlier from the responsible institution counts against my redress payment (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) s 30(2) step 3; Rules s 26)? A payment the responsible institution (or someone on its behalf) made to you for the abuse counts, except a payment under a workers' or military or veterans' compensation Act listed in the Rules, the part not made in recognition of the abuse or its harm, the part for medical, dental or other treatment or other expenses, and a payment only for non-sexual abuse not linked to the sexual abuse. A payment made for two or more responsible institutions together is not worked out here.
GIVEN `paid by or for the responsible institution for abuse it is responsible for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment was made to you by the responsible institution, or on its behalf, in relation to abuse for which it is responsible
      `paid for two or more responsible institutions together` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment was made by one responsible institution on behalf of others (or for it by another responsible institution)
      `under a listed compensation Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was paid under the Safety, Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1988, the listed Parts of the Defence-related Claims Act 1988, the listed Chapters of the Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004, the listed Parts of the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986, or the listed Parts of the British Nuclear Tests (Treatment) Act 2006
      `only for non-sexual abuse not linked to the sexual abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment was only for non-sexual abuse that is not in the same set of abuse (the same responsible institution or institutions) as sexual abuse of you
      `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you were paid, in dollars
      `the part not in recognition of the abuse or its harm` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of it, in dollars, that was not in recognition of the abuse or of harm caused by it (0 if none)
      `the part for treatment or other expenses` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of it, in dollars, reasonably attributable to medical, dental or other treatment or to other expenses such as living expenses (0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much of an earlier payment counts against my redress payment question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `paid by or for the responsible institution for abuse it is responsible for`
              THEN JUST 0
           IF `under a listed compensation Act` OR `only for non-sexual abuse not linked to the sexual abuse`
              THEN JUST 0
           IF `paid for two or more responsible institutions together`
              THEN NOTHING
           OTHERWISE JUST (max 0 ((`the amount paid` MINUS `the part not in recognition of the abuse or its harm`) MINUS `the part for treatment or other expenses`))

DECLARE `My counselling and psychological component` IS ONE OF
    `access to counselling and psychological services provided under the scheme, through my State or Territory (ss 16(1)(b)(i), 51(2))`
    `a counselling and psychological services payment of` HAS `the payment amount` IS A NUMBER

-- s 16(1)(b): "depending on where the person lives (as stated in the person's application for redress)", access to
-- services under the scheme or "a payment (of up to $5,000)". s 51(2): if the place "is in a participating jurisdiction
-- that is a declared provider", the Operator must refer the person and the jurisdiction must provide the services; (3):
-- "If subsection (2) does not apply, then the Operator must, as soon as practicable, pay the counselling and
-- psychological services payment". s 31(2): "The amount must not be more than $5,000".
@export What counselling and psychological help will I get as part of redress (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 16, 31, 51)? If the place where you live (as stated in your application) is in a State or Territory that provides counselling and psychological services under the scheme, you are referred to it for those services. Otherwise you are paid a counselling and psychological services payment worked out under the assessment framework, of at most $5,000. You get it if you choose it when you accept your offer.
GIVEN `I live in a declared provider jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the place where you live, as stated in your application, is in a participating State or Territory that is a declared provider of counselling and psychological services under the scheme
      `the amount under the assessment framework` IS A NUMBER @desc The counselling and psychological component the assessment framework gives you, in dollars (the Act caps it at 5000)
GIVETH A `My counselling and psychological component`
`What counselling and psychological component will I get question` MEANS
    IF `I live in a declared provider jurisdiction`
    THEN `access to counselling and psychological services provided under the scheme, through my State or Territory (ss 16(1)(b)(i), 51(2))`
    ELSE `a counselling and psychological services payment of` (min `the cap on the counselling and psychological component` `the amount under the assessment framework`)

-- s 56B(1): "The Operator may ... pay an amount under this section (an advance payment) for a person if: (a) the person
-- has made an application ...; and (b) the application includes a statement ... that the person has suffered
-- institutional child sexual abuse that occurred: (i) inside a participating State; or (ii) inside a Territory; or (iii)
-- outside Australia; and (c) the person was not prevented under section 20 from making the application; and (d) the
-- Operator has not made a determination under section 29 ...; and (e) the Operator is satisfied that one or more of the
-- following apply: (i) the person is aged 70 or over; (ii) the person is aged 55 or over and is an Aboriginal person or
-- Torres Strait Islander ...; (iii) the person is terminally ill; (iv) there are exceptional circumstances ...; and (f)
-- the person has not died; and (g) the Operator considers it appropriate to do so; and (h) any requirements prescribed by
-- the rules are satisfied." (2): "$10,000". The ages are worked out from the date of birth; the rules prescribe no further
-- circumstance or requirement in the deposited compilation.
@export Can the Operator pay me a $10,000 advance payment while my redress application is being decided (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) s 56B)? It can if you have applied (stating that the abuse happened in a participating State, a Territory or overseas), your application has not yet been decided, you are aged 70 or over, or 55 or over and Aboriginal or Torres Strait Islander, or terminally ill, or there are exceptional circumstances, and the Operator considers it appropriate. The advance payment is taken off your redress payment, and it becomes a debt if you withdraw your application or decline your offer.
GIVEN `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made an application for redress
      `my application states abuse in a participating State, a Territory or overseas` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application states that you suffered institutional child sexual abuse that occurred inside a participating State, inside a Territory, or outside Australia
      `I was prevented from applying under s 20` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were not allowed to make the application (you had already applied, a security notice was in force, you were a child who would not turn 18 before the scheme ends, or you applied in the last 12 months without exceptional circumstances)
      `my application has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator has already decided to approve or not approve your application
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the day the Operator considers it` IS A DATE @desc The day the Operator considers making the advance payment (today, if you are asking now)
      `I am Aboriginal or a Torres Strait Islander` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Aboriginal person or Torres Strait Islander
      `I am terminally ill` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are terminally ill
      `the Operator is satisfied there are exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator is satisfied there are exceptional circumstances justifying an advance payment
      `the Operator considers it appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator considers it appropriate to make the advance payment
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I get an advance payment question` MEANS
    IF      `I have applied`
        AND `my application states abuse in a participating State, a Territory or overseas`
        AND (NOT `I was prevented from applying under s 20`)
        AND (NOT `my application has been decided`)
        AND (   `aged 70 or over`
             OR (`aged 55 or over` AND `I am Aboriginal or a Torres Strait Islander`)
             OR `I am terminally ill`
             OR `the Operator is satisfied there are exceptional circumstances`)
        AND `the Operator considers it appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHERE
        `aged 70 or over` MEANS `the day` `the day the Operator considers it` `is on or after` (`the anniversary` 70 `years after` `my date of birth`)
        `aged 55 or over` MEANS `the day` `the day the Operator considers it` `is on or after` (`the anniversary` 55 `years after` `my date of birth`)

-- s 167(1): an amount paid "is a debt due to the Commonwealth only to the extent expressly provided for by this section".
-- (2): paid to the wrong person (the whole) or more than payable (the excess); (3): the part attributable to a false or
-- misleading statement or misrepresentation; (4): the part attributable to a failure to notify under s 181; (4A): an
-- advance payment, if the person withdraws the application under s 22 or declines the offer under s 45 (which includes
-- being taken to have declined, s 45(2)). Overlapping heads are not added: the largest is taken, capped at the amount
-- paid (fork F7).
@export Must I pay back an amount paid to me under the National Redress Scheme (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) s 167)? An amount is a debt to the Commonwealth only as the Act says: the whole of an advance payment if you withdraw your application or decline (or are taken to have declined) your offer; an amount paid to the wrong person; the part paid above what was payable; the part paid because of a false or misleading statement; and the part paid because you did not tell the Operator something you had to. The answer is the amount in dollars you would owe.
GIVEN `it was an advance payment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the amount was the advance payment
      `I withdrew my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you withdrew your application before it was decided
      `I declined my offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you declined your offer of redress, or are taken to have declined it by not accepting it in time
      `the amount paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount you were paid, in dollars
      `paid to the wrong person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the amount was paid to you when it should have gone to someone else
      `the excess over what was payable` IS A NUMBER @desc How much more than was payable to you was paid, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the part due to a false or misleading statement` IS A NUMBER @desc The part of the amount paid because of a false or misleading statement or misrepresentation, by you or anyone else, in dollars (0 if none)
      `the part due to my not notifying the Operator` IS A NUMBER @desc The part that would not have been payable had you told the Operator something you were required to under s 181, in dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`Must I pay back an amount paid to me question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `it was an advance payment` AND (`I withdrew my application` OR `I declined my offer`)
              THEN `the amount paid`
           IF `paid to the wrong person`
              THEN `the amount paid`
           OTHERWISE min `the amount paid` (max `the excess over what was payable` (max `the part due to a false or misleading statement` `the part due to my not notifying the Operator`))

§§ `My offer of redress (Part 2-4)`

-- s 40(1): "The acceptance period for an offer of redress ... is the period determined by the Operator, which must be at
-- least 6 months, starting on the date of the offer." (2)-(5): the Operator may extend it in exceptional circumstances,
-- on its own initiative or at my request, before the end or after it while I have neither accepted nor declined.
@export By when must I accept my offer of redress (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 40, 42)? You must give the Operator your signed acceptance document before the end of the acceptance period stated in your offer, which must be at least 6 months starting on the date of the offer, or by the end of the period as the Operator has extended it. The answer is the last day you can accept. It is not moved if it falls on a weekend or public holiday. If the period in your offer is shorter than 6 months, there is no answer, because the offer does not meet the Act.
GIVEN `the date of my offer` IS A DATE @desc The date of your offer of redress
      `the last day stated in my offer` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the acceptance period stated in your offer
      `the Operator extended the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator has extended the acceptance period by written notice
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period as extended (if not extended, any date; it is not used)
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must I accept my offer question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day` `the last day stated in my offer` `is before` (`the last day of the` 6 `month period starting on` `the date of my offer`)
              THEN NOTHING
           IF `the Operator extended the period` AND `the day` `the extended last day` `is after` `the last day stated in my offer`
              THEN JUST `the extended last day`
           OTHERWISE JUST `the last day stated in my offer`

-- s 42(3): "The person must give the Operator the acceptance document: (a) before the end of the acceptance period". As a
-- regulative rule, counted in days from the date of the offer to the last day of the acceptance period.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Redress party` `Redress step`
`s 42(3) -- I must give my acceptance document before the end of the acceptance period` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I, the survivor applying for redress`
    DO `give the Operator my acceptance document`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I, the survivor applying for redress` BECAUSE "no acceptance before the end of the acceptance period: I am taken to have declined the offer (s 45(2)), unless my review was not completed at the end of the period (s 45(3)); the Operator may still extend the period while I have neither accepted nor declined (s 40(4A)(b), (6))"

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 42(3) -- an acceptance on this day is in time` `the days allowed` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 42(3) -- I must give my acceptance document before the end of the acceptance period` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `I, the survivor applying for redress` `give the Operator my acceptance document` `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Where my offer stands` IS ONE OF
    `accepted: I am entitled to redress, and the release from civil liability in s 43 has taken effect (ss 12(2)(e), 42, 43)`
    `declined: I declined in writing before the end of the acceptance period; I get no redress and release no one, and cannot apply again (s 45(1))`
    `open: I can still accept or decline until the end of the acceptance period (s 40)`
    `not taken to have declined: my review was not completed at the end of the acceptance period (s 45(3))`
    `taken to have declined: I did not accept before the end of the acceptance period (s 45(2)); the Operator may still extend the period (s 40(4A)(b), (6))`

@export Where does my offer of redress stand: accepted, declined, still open, or taken to have been declined (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 40, 42, 43, 45)? You accept by giving the Operator a signed acceptance document before the end of the acceptance period; you decline by giving a signed declining document, or by doing nothing until the period ends. Doing nothing does not count as declining while a review you applied for is not completed at the end of the period. Accepting releases the responsible institutions and their officials (but not the abuser) from civil liability for the abuse.
GIVEN `the date of my offer` IS A DATE @desc The date of your offer of redress
      `the last day of my acceptance period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of your acceptance period, as stated in the offer or as extended
      `I gave an acceptance document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Operator a signed acceptance document in the approved form
      `I gave it on` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave it (if not, any date; it is not used)
      `I gave a declining document` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have given the Operator a signed document in the approved form declining the offer
      `I declined on` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave it (if not, any date; it is not used)
      `my review was not completed at the end of the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied for review of the Operator's determination and the review was not completed by the end of the acceptance period
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Where my offer stands`
`Where does my offer of redress stand question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `accepted in time` AND ((NOT `declined in time`) OR `the day` `I gave it on` `is before` `I declined on`)
              THEN `accepted: I am entitled to redress, and the release from civil liability in s 43 has taken effect (ss 12(2)(e), 42, 43)`
           IF `declined in time`
              THEN `declined: I declined in writing before the end of the acceptance period; I get no redress and release no one, and cannot apply again (s 45(1))`
           IF `the day` `today` `is on or before` `the last day of my acceptance period`
              THEN `open: I can still accept or decline until the end of the acceptance period (s 40)`
           IF `my review was not completed at the end of the period`
              THEN `not taken to have declined: my review was not completed at the end of the acceptance period (s 45(3))`
           OTHERWISE `taken to have declined: I did not accept before the end of the acceptance period (s 45(2)); the Operator may still extend the period (s 40(4A)(b), (6))`
    WHERE
        `accepted in time` MEANS
                `I gave an acceptance document`
            AND `s 42(3) -- an acceptance on this day is in time` (`the days from` `the date of my offer` `to` `the last day of my acceptance period`) (`the days from` `the date of my offer` `to` `I gave it on`)
        `declined in time` MEANS
                `I gave a declining document`
            AND `the day` `I declined on` `is on or before` `the last day of my acceptance period`

DECLARE `Who I might sue for the abuse` IS ONE OF
    `a participating institution the Operator determined is responsible for my abuse`
    `a participating institution identified in my offer as an associate of a responsible institution`
    `an official of one of those institutions who is not my abuser`
    `my abuser`
    `an institution listed under s 164, 164A, 164B or 164C (a funder of last resort case)`
    `another institution or person`

-- s 43: on acceptance "(a) the person releases and forever discharges every released institution or official from civil
-- liability for abuse of the person that is within the scope of the scheme; and (b) the person cannot ... bring or
-- continue civil proceedings against a released institution or official in relation to that abuse; and (c) the release
-- ... does not: (i) release or discharge another institution or person ...; and (ii) prevent the person ... from bringing
-- or continuing civil proceedings against another institution or person". s 42(2)(c): the released institutions and
-- officials are the responsible participating institutions, their associates identified in the offer, and their officials
-- "(other than an official who is an abuser of the person)". Rules s 31 note 3: listed institutions are not released.
@export If I accept my offer of redress, can I still sue for the abuse (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 42, 43)? Accepting releases for ever the participating institutions the Operator found responsible, the associates named in your offer, and their officials, from civil liability for the abuse, and you cannot bring or continue a claim against them. You can still sue your abuser and any other institution or person. If you sue another party, any contribution a released institution would have owed is taken off your damages.
GIVEN `I have accepted my offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have accepted an offer of redress by giving your acceptance document in time
      `who` IS A `Who I might sue for the abuse` @desc Who you want to sue for the abuse: a responsible participating institution; an associate named in your offer; an official of those institutions who is not your abuser; your abuser; an institution listed for a funder of last resort; or another institution or person
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still sue for the abuse after accepting redress question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF NOT `I have accepted my offer`
              THEN NOTHING
           IF     `who` EQUALS `a participating institution the Operator determined is responsible for my abuse`
               OR `who` EQUALS `a participating institution identified in my offer as an associate of a responsible institution`
               OR `who` EQUALS `an official of one of those institutions who is not my abuser`
              THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 12(2): "A person is entitled to redress under the scheme if: (a) the person applies ...; and (b) the Operator
-- considers that there is a reasonable likelihood that the person is eligible ...; and (c) the Operator approves the
-- application ...; and (d) the Operator makes an offer ...; and (e) the person accepts the offer in accordance with
-- section 42." (4): "not entitled ... if this Act or the rules prescribe". s 64: "not entitled ... while a security notice
-- is in force". s 63(2): not entitled for the listed sentences or after a special assessment determination, unless a
-- s 63(5) determination is in force.
@export Am I entitled to redress under the National Redress Scheme (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 12, 63, 64)? You are entitled once you have applied, the Operator has found a reasonable likelihood that you are eligible and approved your application, made you an offer, and you have accepted it in time with a signed acceptance document. You are not entitled while a security notice is in force, or if your prison sentence takes you out of the scheme (see the question about sentences).
GIVEN `I applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you applied for redress
      `the Operator found a reasonable likelihood` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator considers there is a reasonable likelihood that you are eligible
      `my application was approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator approved your application (or a review approved it)
      `I was made an offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator made you an offer of redress
      `I accepted in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you accepted the offer by giving the signed acceptance document before the end of the acceptance period
      `a security notice is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a security notice is in force in relation to you
      `my sentence takes me out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether s 63 makes you not entitled because of a sentence of 5 years or longer (see the question about sentences)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Am I entitled to redress question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `a security notice is in force` OR `my sentence takes me out`
              THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `I applied` AND `the Operator found a reasonable likelihood` AND `my application was approved` AND `I was made an offer` AND `I accepted in time`
              THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `The offence I was sentenced for` IS ONE OF
    `unlawful killing, or an attempt or conspiracy to commit one`
    `a sexual offence, or an offence that includes the intention to commit one`
    `a terrorism offence within the meaning of the Crimes Act 1914`
    `a State, Territory or foreign offence the Operator is satisfied is substantially similar to a terrorism offence`
    `another offence`

DECLARE `What my sentence means for redress` IS ONE OF
    `s 63 does not apply: I have not been sentenced to imprisonment for 5 years or longer`
    `not prevented: a determination under s 63(5) that I am not prevented is in force`
    `not entitled: the sentence is for an offence listed in s 63(2)(a), unless the Operator determines under s 63(5) that I am not prevented`
    `not entitled: the Operator has determined that I should undergo a special assessment process (s 63(2B)), unless it determines under s 63(5) that I am not prevented`
    `not prevented by s 63 on these facts: the Operator must consider whether I should undergo a special assessment process (s 63(2A))`

-- s 63(1): applies if "before or after making the application, the person is sentenced to imprisonment for 5 years or
-- longer for an offence against a law of the Commonwealth, a State, a Territory or a foreign country". (2): not entitled
-- if the sentence is for the listed offences, or the Operator has determined a special assessment under (2B), "unless
-- there is a determination in force under subsection (5)". (2A): otherwise the Operator must consider a special
-- assessment. (5): "The Operator may determine that the person is not prevented ... if ... satisfied that providing
-- redress ... would not: (a) bring the scheme into disrepute; or (b) adversely affect public confidence in, or support
-- for, the scheme."
@export Does a prison sentence stop me getting redress (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) s 63)? If you have been sentenced to imprisonment for 5 years or longer for unlawful killing, a sexual offence or a terrorism offence, or the Operator decides that you should undergo a special assessment process because of your sentence, you are not entitled to redress unless the Operator decides that redress for you would not bring the scheme into disrepute or harm public confidence in it. Advice from the Attorney-General of the place of the abuse is given greater weight.
GIVEN `my sentence of imprisonment in years` IS A NUMBER @desc The length of the sentence of imprisonment you received, in years (0 if none)
      `the offence` IS A `The offence I was sentenced for` @desc What the sentence was for: unlawful killing (or an attempt or conspiracy); a sexual offence; a Commonwealth terrorism offence; a State, Territory or foreign offence the Operator is satisfied is substantially similar to one; or another offence
      `the Operator determined a special assessment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator has determined that you should undergo a special assessment process
      `a not-prevented determination is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator has determined under s 63(5) that you are not prevented from being entitled to redress, and that determination is in force
GIVETH A `What my sentence means for redress`
`Does my prison sentence stop me getting redress question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `my sentence of imprisonment in years` LESS THAN 5
              THEN `s 63 does not apply: I have not been sentenced to imprisonment for 5 years or longer`
           IF `a not-prevented determination is in force`
              THEN `not prevented: a determination under s 63(5) that I am not prevented is in force`
           IF NOT (`the offence` EQUALS `another offence`)
              THEN `not entitled: the sentence is for an offence listed in s 63(2)(a), unless the Operator determines under s 63(5) that I am not prevented`
           IF `the Operator determined a special assessment`
              THEN `not entitled: the Operator has determined that I should undergo a special assessment process (s 63(2B)), unless it determines under s 63(5) that I am not prevented`
           OTHERWISE `not prevented by s 63 on these facts: the Operator must consider whether I should undergo a special assessment process (s 63(2A))`

§§ `Review of the Operator's determination (Part 4-1)`

-- s 73(2): the application for review "must: (a) be made before the day specified in the notice of the determination
-- given under section 34". s 34(4): if approved, "the review period ... is the same as the acceptance period"; (6): if not
-- approved, the period "determined by the Operator, which must: (a) start on the date of the notice; and (b) be at least
-- 28 days, but not longer than 6 months". As a regulative rule, counted in days from the date of the notice to the last
-- day of the review period (fork F3: "before the day specified" read as by the last day of the period specified).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Redress party` `Redress step`
`s 73(2)(a) -- I must apply for review within the review period` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `I, the survivor applying for redress`
    DO `apply for review of the Operator's determination`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `I, the survivor applying for redress` BECAUSE "no application for review within the review period (s 73(2)(a)); if approved, the Operator may extend the acceptance period and with it the review period (ss 34(5), 40(2), (4A)); if not approved, it may extend the review period in exceptional circumstances, even after it has ended (s 34(7)-(10))"

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER, `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 73(2)(a) -- a review application on this day is in time` `the days allowed` `the day` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE (`s 73(2)(a) -- I must apply for review within the review period` `the days allowed`) 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the day`), (EVENT `I, the survivor applying for redress` `apply for review of the Operator's determination` `the day`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Whether my review application is in time` IS ONE OF
    `in time (s 73(2)(a))`
    `late: my application was approved, so the review period is my acceptance period; I can ask the Operator to extend the acceptance period, which extends the review period, while I have neither accepted nor declined (ss 34(4), (5), 40(2), (4A))`
    `late: my application was not approved; I can ask the Operator to extend the review period in exceptional circumstances, even after it has ended (s 34(7)-(10))`

@export Am I in time to apply for review of the Operator's decision on my redress application (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 34, 73)? If your application was approved, the review period is the same as your acceptance period (as extended). If it was not approved, it is the period stated in the notice, which must be at least 28 days and at most 6 months from the date of the notice. If you are late, the Operator can extend the period. Enter the last day of the period as stated in your notice or as extended.
GIVEN `my application was approved` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Operator approved your application
      `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date of the Operator's notice of its decision on your application
      `the last day of my review period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the review period: if approved, the last day of your acceptance period (as extended); if not approved, the last day stated in the notice (as extended)
      `applying on` IS A DATE @desc The day you apply, or would apply, for review
GIVETH A `Whether my review application is in time`
`Am I in time to apply for review question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `s 73(2)(a) -- a review application on this day is in time` (`the days from` `the date of the notice` `to` `the last day of my review period`) (`the days from` `the date of the notice` `to` `applying on`)
              THEN `in time (s 73(2)(a))`
           IF `my application was approved`
              THEN `late: my application was approved, so the review period is my acceptance period; I can ask the Operator to extend the acceptance period, which extends the review period, while I have neither accepted nor declined (ss 34(4), (5), 40(2), (4A))`
           OTHERWISE `late: my application was not approved; I can ask the Operator to extend the review period in exceptional circumstances, even after it has ended (s 34(7)-(10))`

DECLARE `Whether my review period meets the Act` IS ONE OF
    `it meets the Act: at least 28 days and not longer than 6 months, starting on the date of the notice (s 34(6))`
    `too short: it ends before the 28th day starting on the date of the notice (s 34(6)(b))`
    `too long: it ends after the last day of 6 months starting on the date of the notice (s 34(6)(b))`

@export My redress application was not approved: is the review period in my notice as long as the Act requires (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) s 34(6))? The period the Operator sets must start on the date of the notice and be at least 28 days but not longer than 6 months. The Operator may later extend it in exceptional circumstances.
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE @desc The date of the notice telling you your application was not approved
      `the last day stated in the notice` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the review period stated in the notice
GIVETH A `Whether my review period meets the Act`
`Is my review period as long as the Act requires question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day` `the last day stated in the notice` `is before` (`the date` 27 `days after` `the date of the notice`)
              THEN `too short: it ends before the 28th day starting on the date of the notice (s 34(6)(b))`
           IF `the day` `the last day stated in the notice` `is after` (`the last day of the` 6 `month period starting on` `the date of the notice`)
              THEN `too long: it ends after the last day of 6 months starting on the date of the notice (s 34(6)(b))`
           OTHERWISE `it meets the Act: at least 28 days and not longer than 6 months, starting on the date of the notice (s 34(6))`

-- s 75(4): "The review determination must not have the effect of reducing the amount of the redress payment determined
-- in the original determination, unless the reviewer is satisfied that: (a) either: (i) the reduction is the result of
-- considering information mentioned in paragraph (3)(b) or (c) [information with the review application, or requested for
-- the review]; or (ii) the Operator has reasonable grounds to believe that information given ... is false or misleading in
-- a material particular; and (b) the reduction is appropriate, having regard to the principles set out in section 10."
@export Can a review of my redress decision reduce my redress payment (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) s 75(4))? A review must not reduce the amount unless the reviewer is satisfied that the reduction comes from new information given with your review application or asked for during the review, or that the Operator has reasonable grounds to believe information given was false or misleading, and that the reduction is appropriate having regard to the scheme's survivor-focussed principles.
GIVEN `it results from information given or asked for in the review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the reviewer is satisfied the reduction results from considering information that came with your review application, or that the reviewer asked you or an institution for during the review
      `the Operator believes information was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the reviewer is satisfied the Operator has reasonable grounds to believe information, a document or a statement given for your application or review was false or misleading in a material particular
      `the reviewer is satisfied the reduction is appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the reviewer is satisfied the reduction is appropriate, having regard to the guiding principles in s 10 (survivor-focussed, avoiding further harm, protecting the scheme's integrity)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the review reduce my redress payment question` MEANS
    IF     (`it results from information given or asked for in the review` OR `the Operator believes information was false or misleading`)
       AND `the reviewer is satisfied the reduction is appropriate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

DECLARE `The review outcome` IS ONE OF
    `the review affirmed the determination`
    `the review varied the determination`
    `the review set the determination aside and substituted a new one`

DECLARE `What happens after my review` IS ONE OF
    `my review was taken to be withdrawn when I accepted or declined my offer (s 78(2))`
    `the acceptance period is extended by an additional 2 months; its new last day is` HAS `the new last day` IS A DATE
    `my offer is withdrawn and I get a new written offer (s 78(3))`
    `my offer is withdrawn, and I get no new offer because the determination no longer approves my application (s 78(3)(a))`
    `I get an offer of redress, as the determination now approves my application (ss 39, 76(3))`
    `the decision not to approve my application stands (s 75(2)(b)(i))`
    `the determination is changed, and still does not approve my application (s 76(3))`

-- s 78(2): accepting or declining before the review is completed withdraws the review. (3): if varied or substituted, the
-- Operator must "(a) withdraw the offer ...; and (b) if the determination as varied or substituted approves the
-- application--give the person a new written offer". (4): if affirmed, approving, with an offer given, "the Operator
-- must extend the acceptance period under subsection 40(2) for an additional 2 months" (read as the 2 months starting on
-- the day after the old last day). s 76(3): the varied or substituted determination is taken to be the s 29 determination.
@export What happens to my offer of redress when my review is decided (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 76, 78)? If the review confirms an approval, your acceptance period is extended by 2 more months. If the review changes the decision, your offer is withdrawn and, if your application is still or now approved, you get a new offer. If you accepted or declined your offer before the review finished, the review was taken to be withdrawn.
GIVEN `the outcome` IS A `The review outcome` @desc What the review decided: affirmed, varied, or set aside and substituted the Operator's determination
      `the determination as it now stands approves my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the determination, as affirmed, varied or substituted, approves your application for redress
      `I had been given an offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had been given an offer of redress before the review was decided
      `I accepted or declined before the review was completed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you accepted or declined that offer before the review was completed
      `the last day of my acceptance period` IS A DATE @desc The last day of your acceptance period before the review was decided (if no offer, any date; it is not used)
GIVETH A `What happens after my review`
`What happens to my offer after my review question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `I had been given an offer` AND `I accepted or declined before the review was completed`
              THEN `my review was taken to be withdrawn when I accepted or declined my offer (s 78(2))`
           IF `the outcome` EQUALS `the review affirmed the determination` AND `the determination as it now stands approves my application` AND `I had been given an offer`
              THEN `the acceptance period is extended by an additional 2 months; its new last day is` (`the last day of the` 2 `month period starting on` (`the date` 1 `days after` `the last day of my acceptance period`))
           IF `the outcome` EQUALS `the review affirmed the determination`
              THEN `the decision not to approve my application stands (s 75(2)(b)(i))`
           IF `I had been given an offer` AND `the determination as it now stands approves my application`
              THEN `my offer is withdrawn and I get a new written offer (s 78(3))`
           IF `I had been given an offer`
              THEN `my offer is withdrawn, and I get no new offer because the determination no longer approves my application (s 78(3)(a))`
           IF `the determination as it now stands approves my application`
              THEN `I get an offer of redress, as the determination now approves my application (ss 39, 76(3))`
           OTHERWISE `the determination is changed, and still does not approve my application (s 76(3))`

§§ `Once I have accepted (Part 2-5)`

DECLARE `The institution I want a direct personal response from` IS ONE OF
    `a participating institution the Operator determined is responsible`
    `a partly-participating institution the Operator determined is responsible, with a participating jurisdiction as funder of last resort`
    `a defunct institution (a funder of last resort case)`
    `another institution listed under s 164A or 164C`

-- s 54(1): "If a participating institution or partly-participating institution is given a notice under section 44, 46B
-- or 71L that notifies the institution that a person wishes to be given a direct personal response from the institution,
-- then the institution must take reasonable steps to provide the person with a direct personal response." (2): an
-- apology or statement of acknowledgement or regret; acknowledgement of the impact; an assurance about prevention; an
-- opportunity to meet a senior official. s 39(i)(iii), (ia)(iv): a direct personal response "is not available" for abuse
-- for which a defunct institution is responsible.
@export Must the institution give me a direct personal response, such as an apology or a meeting (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 16, 39, 42, 54)? If you accept your offer and say in your acceptance document that you want a direct personal response from a responsible participating institution (or a partly-participating institution with a funder of last resort), it must take reasonable steps to give you one: an apology or statement of regret, an acknowledgement of the abuse's impact on you, an assurance about preventing abuse, or a meeting with a senior official. None is available from a defunct institution.
GIVEN `I accepted and asked for a response from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you accepted your offer and named this institution in your acceptance document as one you want a direct personal response from
      `the institution` IS A `The institution I want a direct personal response from` @desc Which kind of institution it is: a responsible participating institution; a responsible partly-participating institution with a funder of last resort; a defunct institution; or another listed institution
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must the institution give me a direct personal response question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the institution` EQUALS `a defunct institution (a funder of last resort case)`
              THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the institution` EQUALS `another institution listed under s 164A or 164C`
              THEN NOTHING
           IF `I accepted and asked for a response from it`
              THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `The scheme payment` IS ONE OF
    `my redress payment`
    `my counselling and psychological services payment`
    `my advance payment`

DECLARE `Where the payment would be counted` IS ONE OF
    `the Social Security Act 1991 or the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986`
    `any other Commonwealth, State or Territory legislation`
    `a liability insurance contract`

-- ss 49(1), 52(1), 56C(1): the payment "is a payment of compensation under the scheme. However, for the purposes of: (a)
-- the Social Security Act 1991 and the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986; and (b) any other legislation of the
-- Commonwealth, a State or a Territory; the payment is not to be treated as being a payment of compensation or damages."
-- ss 49(3), 52(3), 56C(4): "Nothing in this Act prevents a liability insurance contract from treating" it as compensation
-- or damages.
@export Is my redress payment treated as compensation or damages for social security, veterans' entitlements or other laws (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 49, 52, 56C)? No: a redress payment, counselling and psychological services payment or advance payment is not treated as compensation or damages under the Social Security Act, the Veterans' Entitlements Act or any other Commonwealth, State or Territory legislation, so it does not reduce those payments. It cannot be sold, assigned, charged or taken in bankruptcy, and nothing may be deducted from it. The Act does not stop a liability insurance contract treating it as compensation.
GIVEN `the payment` IS A `The scheme payment` @desc Which payment: your redress payment, your counselling and psychological services payment, or your advance payment
      `where` IS A `Where the payment would be counted` @desc Where the question arises: the Social Security Act or Veterans' Entitlements Act; any other Commonwealth, State or Territory law; or a liability insurance contract
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my redress payment treated as compensation question` MEANS
    IF `where` EQUALS `a liability insurance contract`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- ss 50(2), 53(2), 56D(2): "Step 1. Work out the amount of the ... payment that has been paid to the credit of the
-- account in the year immediately before the court order came into force. Step 2. Subtract from the amount of that
-- payment the total amount withdrawn from the account during that year: the result is the saved amount." (1): a
-- garnishee order "does not apply to the saved amount (if any)".
@export How much of my bank account is protected from a garnishee order because it holds my redress payment (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 50, 53, 56D)? The protected (saved) amount is the redress, counselling or advance payment paid into the account in the year before the court order came into force, less everything withdrawn from the account in that year. If the withdrawals are larger, nothing is protected.
GIVEN `paid into the account in the year before the order` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount of the payment (all instalments) paid into the account in the year immediately before the garnishee order came into force, in dollars
      `withdrawn from the account in that year` IS A NUMBER @desc The total withdrawn from the account in that year, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my account is protected from a garnishee order question` MEANS
    max 0 (`paid into the account in the year before the order` MINUS `withdrawn from the account in that year`)

DECLARE `The document` IS ONE OF
    `my application for redress`
    `a document created solely to accompany my application`
    `a document created solely to answer the Operator's request for information`
    `another document`

DECLARE `The proceedings` IS ONE OF
    `civil proceedings to give effect to the Act, including judicial review of a decision under it`
    `other civil proceedings in a court or tribunal`
    `criminal proceedings`

-- s 37(1): "The following documents are not admissible in evidence in civil proceedings in a court or tribunal: (a) a
-- person's application for redress; (b) a document created solely for the purposes of accompanying a person's
-- application ...; (c) a document created solely for the purposes of complying with a request for information made by
-- the Operator under section 24 or 25". (2), (3): not where the admission "is for the purposes of giving effect to this
-- Act", including judicial review of a decision under it.
@export Can my redress application, or documents made for it, be used as evidence in civil proceedings (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) s 37)? Your application, a document made only to go with it, and a document made only to answer the Operator's request for information are not admissible in civil proceedings in a court or tribunal, unless the proceedings are to give effect to the Act (such as judicial review of a decision under it). The Act says nothing here about criminal proceedings or other documents.
GIVEN `the document` IS A `The document` @desc Which document: your application; a document made only to go with it; a document made only to answer the Operator's request for information; or another document
      `the proceedings` IS A `The proceedings` @desc What proceedings: civil proceedings to give effect to the Act (including judicial review of a decision under it); other civil proceedings; or criminal proceedings
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can my redress documents be used as evidence question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the document` EQUALS `another document` OR `the proceedings` EQUALS `criminal proceedings`
              THEN NOTHING
           IF `the proceedings` EQUALS `other civil proceedings in a court or tribunal`
              THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§§ `If the applicant dies before accepting (Part 3-1 Division 2; a situation the family may be in)`

DECLARE `When the applicant died` IS ONE OF
    `before the Operator decided the application`
    `after being given an offer, before accepting, declining or its withdrawal`
    `after accepting the offer`
    `after declining the offer`

DECLARE `What happens to the redress payment` IS ONE OF
    `the application continues; if approved, the redress payment is paid to the people the Operator determines (ss 58, 60)`
    `the offer is withdrawn; the redress payment is paid to the people the Operator determines (ss 59(2), (3), 60)`
    `the offer is withdrawn; the review continues, and if it approves the application the redress payment is paid to the people the Operator determines (ss 59(2), (4), 60)`
    `the redress payment, or any unpaid instalments, is still paid, to an account the executor or administrator nominates if the applicant's own account can no longer be used (s 48(1D); Rules s 33(3))`
    `nothing is payable: the offer was declined (s 45)`

-- s 58: if the applicant dies before a determination, "The Operator must continue to deal with the application as if the
-- person had not died" and the redress payment is payable under s 60. s 59(2): an offer outstanding at death "is taken to
-- be withdrawn immediately after the person dies"; (3): payable under s 60 if there was no review or it was completed;
-- (4): a pending review "continues as if the person had not died". s 60(2), (3): the Operator determines who is paid,
-- and "may consider the people who are entitled to the property of the deceased person under: (a) the deceased person's
-- will; and (b) the law relating to the disposition of the property of deceased persons"; (4): without probate or letters
-- of administration. Only the redress payment passes, not the counselling component or a direct personal response.
@export The person who applied for redress has died: what happens to the redress payment (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) ss 48, 58-60; Rules s 33)? If they died before the application was decided, it continues, and if approved the redress payment is paid to the people the Operator decides, who may be those entitled under the will or the law of intestacy, without needing probate. If they died holding an offer, the offer is withdrawn and the payment goes the same way (after any pending review). If they had accepted, the payment is still made. If they had declined, nothing is payable.
GIVEN `when they died` IS A `When the applicant died` @desc When the applicant died: before the application was decided; after an offer but before accepting, declining or its withdrawal; after accepting; or after declining
      `a review was pending when they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the applicant had applied for review of the Operator's determination and the review was not completed when they died
GIVETH A `What happens to the redress payment`
`What happens to the redress payment if the applicant dies question` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `when they died` EQUALS `before the Operator decided the application`
              THEN `the application continues; if approved, the redress payment is paid to the people the Operator determines (ss 58, 60)`
           IF `when they died` EQUALS `after accepting the offer`
              THEN `the redress payment, or any unpaid instalments, is still paid, to an account the executor or administrator nominates if the applicant's own account can no longer be used (s 48(1D); Rules s 33(3))`
           IF `when they died` EQUALS `after declining the offer`
              THEN `nothing is payable: the offer was declined (s 45)`
           IF `a review was pending when they died`
              THEN `the offer is withdrawn; the review continues, and if it approves the application the redress payment is paid to the people the Operator determines (ss 59(2), (4), 60)`
           OTHERWISE `the offer is withdrawn; the redress payment is paid to the people the Operator determines (ss 59(2), (3), 60)`

§§ `False or misleading information (s 28)`

-- s 28: "A person must not give information, produce a document or make a statement to an officer of the scheme if the
-- person knows, or is reckless as to whether, the information, document or statement is false or misleading in a
-- material particular." "Civil penalty: 60 penalty units." The value of a penalty unit is set by the Crimes Act 1914
-- s 4AA, which is not deposited; the answer is in penalty units.
@export What is the most I can be ordered to pay for giving false or misleading information to the National Redress Scheme (National Redress Scheme for Institutional Child Sexual Abuse Act 2018 (Cth) s 28)? Knowingly or recklessly giving false or misleading information, documents or statements to an officer of the scheme carries a civil penalty of up to 60 penalty units (the dollar value of a penalty unit is set by the Crimes Act 1914). It may also be a criminal offence under the Criminal Code. The answer is in penalty units; if you did not know and were not reckless, the section does not apply.
GIVEN `I knew or was reckless that it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you knew, or were reckless about whether, the information, document or statement was false or misleading in a material particular
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most I can be ordered to pay for false information question` MEANS
    IF `I knew or was reckless that it was false or misleading`
    THEN 60
    ELSE 0
